Place 1 into image.
Place 1 into image.
Place 0 into image.
Place 1 into image.
Place 0 into image.
Place 1 into image.
Keep a shared rows as 0.
Set rows to 3.
Keep a shared columns as 0.
Set columns to 3.
Keep a shared old as 0.
The start is 4.
Set old to item start of image.
Keep a shared color as 0.
Set color to 2.
Keep a shared queue as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared count as 0.
Keep a shared front as 0.
To expand from node (a whole number).
The row is node divided by columns.
The column is node modulo columns.
The up is node minus columns.
The down is node plus columns.
The left is node minus 1.
The right is node plus 1.
If row is more than 0 and item up of image is old, set item up of image to color, Place up into queue, add 1 to count.
If row is less than rows minus 1 and item down of image is old, set item down of image to color, Place down into queue, add 1 to count.
If column is more than 0 and item left of image is old, set item left of image to color, Place left into queue, add 1 to count.
If column is less than columns minus 1 and item right of image is old, set item right of image to color, Place right into queue, add 1 to count.

If old is not color.
Set item start of image to color.
Place start into queue.
Set count to 1.

Repeat while front is less than count.
The spot is front.
The node is item spot of queue.
Add 1 to front.
Expand from node.

For each value in image, show value.
